CON-02: do not let MinSurfArea override a smaller storage unit's own area

setNodeDepth() floored every node's surface area at MinSurfArea (12.566 ft2
by default) before dy = dV / surfArea, storage units included, while their
volume is node_getVolume() of their own area curve. For a storage unit
smaller than MinSurfArea the depth rose as if it had 12.566 ft2 and the
booked volume lost the difference. For a storage unit, cap the floor at its
own area at full depth: a unit smaller than MinSurfArea uses its real area,
and a curve that starts at zero area keeps the MinSurfArea floor until its
area exceeds it, as before. Junctions and storage units at least
MinSurfArea in size are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-02_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c b/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
index 972da8c..404988f 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/dynwave.c
@@ -652,6 +652,8 @@ void setNodeDepth(int i, double dt)
     double  denom;                     // denominator term
     double  corr;                      // correction factor
     double  f;                         // relative surcharge depth
+    double  aMin;                      // min. surface area (ft2)
+    double  aFull;                     // storage unit area at full depth (ft2)
 
     // --- see if node can pond water above it
     canPond = (AllowPonding && Node[i].pondedArea > 0.0);
@@ -663,7 +665,15 @@ void setNodeDepth(int i, double dt)
     yLast = Node[i].newDepth;
     Node[i].overflow = 0.0;
     surfArea = Xnode[i].newSurfArea;
-    surfArea = MAX(surfArea, MinSurfArea);
+    aMin = MinSurfArea;
+
+    // --- MinSurfArea does not override a smaller storage unit's own area
+    if ( Node[i].type == STORAGE )
+    {
+        aFull = node_getSurfArea(i, Node[i].fullDepth);
+        if ( aFull > 0.0 ) aMin = MIN(aMin, aFull);
+    }
+    surfArea = MAX(surfArea, aMin);
     
     // --- determine average net flow volume into node over the time step
     dQ = Node[i].inflow - Node[i].outflow;
